#
# The ATS3 (ATS-Xanadu) test corpus, ported to ATS2.
#
# The programs here are ports of the tests of the ATS3
# distribution:
#
#   prelude/TEST/CATS/{JS,CM,PY}       ->  prelude/
#   srcgen2/xats2cc/srcgen1/TEST       ->  xats2cc/
#   xatslib/githwxi/TEST/CATS/JS       ->  xatslib/
#
# The ATS3 tests of the three backends (JS, CM and PY) are the
# same programs, so they are ported once.
#
# Every test is a small program that exercises one part of the
# library; its expected output is in the corresponding
# [*.test-cmp] file, and it is run by [make regress].
#
# The output of the original ATS3 programs (obtained by running
# the JavaScript that the ATS3 compiler emits under node) is in
# [goldens/prelude]; it is the reference that the ports were
# written against.  The output of the ports is not always the
# same as the output of the ATS3 programs, because the two
# languages print their values differently; [MAPPING.txt] says
# where they differ.
#

######

The ported programs:

  prelude/      the tests of the ATS3 prelude (12 programs)
  xats2cc/      the tests of the ATS3 C backend (12 programs)
  xatslib/      the tests of the ATS3 xatslib (5 programs)

######

The shim:

  shim/xats3shim.hats

is the ATS2 counterpart of the parts of the ATS3 prelude that
have no counterpart in ATS2: the generic sequence layer
([GSEQ] and [GASQ]), the debugging layer ([gdbg]) and a few
string operations.  It is included by the programs that need
it:

  #include "../shim/xats3shim.hats"

######

How to run the tests:

  make -C doc/EXAMPLE/ATS3PORT/prelude regress
  make -C doc/EXAMPLE/ATS3PORT/xats2cc regress
  make -C doc/EXAMPLE/ATS3PORT/xatslib regress

or, all at once:

  make -C doc -f Makefile_test testall

######

###### end of [README] ######
